course: dictionary
lesson: 658
title: Baggy and loose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how something fits or hangs. Baggy is one of them. Baggy things are big and loose, not tight on your body. Look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «That, says the story, is why rhinos have baggy, folded skin and a very bad temper.» Skin that hangs in loose folds is baggy skin. The word tells you the skin is loose, not tight and smooth.
explain: Baggy can describe more than clothes. Baggy skin under the eyes hangs loosely, often because someone is tired or old. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Baggy means big and loose, not tight on your body.
fact: Baggy jeans and baggy jumpers are comfy because they leave plenty of room to move.
fact: Baggy eyes are skin under the eyes that hangs loosely, often when someone is tired.
fact: Baggies is an informal word for loose trousers.
fact: Very baggy clothes can catch on things like bike chains, so they can be a safety risk.
exercise: «That, says the story, is why rhinos have baggy, folded skin and a very bad temper.» What does baggy mean here? | Tight and smooth | Bright and shiny | Wet and sticky | *Big and loose, hanging in folds
exercise: Which clothes are baggy? | A tight pair of leggings | A pair of trainers laced up tight | *Jeans and a jumper that are much too big for you | A pair of gloves that fit well
exercise: Find and copy the word that means loose and big in this sentence: «Her baggy jumper hung down past her knees.» | jumper | knees | *baggy | hung
test: Baggy eyes are a sign of what? | Being very excited | Being hungry | *Being tired | Being cold
test: Mum says your new trousers are baggy. What does she mean? | They are very dirty | They are shiny and new | They are tight and short | *They are big and loose on your legs
exam: «His writing was so baggy that nobody could read it.» What does baggy mean in this sentence? | Tight, neat and clear | Wet through | *Too long and loose, not tight and clear | Bright and colourful
